WEBVTT

00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:16,800
I was tested for Hashimoto's about 27 years ago and had the antibody. So Hashimoto's is when

00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:22,800
you develop antibodies to the thyroid globulin cells so you got thyroid globulin antibodies

00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:31,520
or thyroid globulin proxidase cells which are TPO antibodies. So those are two different antibodies

00:00:31,520 --> 00:00:37,360
that you would test in a person's blood and if they were elevated you have Hashimoto's.

00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:44,400
Well you have either Hashimoto's or Graves' disease. So if you have spike T3

00:00:45,760 --> 00:00:52,240
be strongly elevated T3 with elevated TPO or thyroid globulin antibodies then you have

00:00:52,240 --> 00:01:01,040
Graves' disease. If you have normal or low T3 then you have Hashimoto's. So it's very

00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:09,280
common in Hashimoto's. So I hadn't been tested again until last May or did not have any antibodies.

00:01:09,280 --> 00:01:15,120
The doctor told me that I either never had it or I had it under control very well.

00:01:16,160 --> 00:01:21,840
Just recently I read that if you have cancer diagnosis these antibodies don't show up as this truth.

00:01:22,320 --> 00:01:32,560
No, I don't think that's true. I've never read anything about that. If you have your Hashimoto's

00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:39,120
under control your antibodies can go back down to normal. So if you ever had elevated antibodies you

00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:46,880
definitely had Hashimoto's. But remember autoimmune disease is diagnosed in three phases. So if you

00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:52,800
have elevated antibodies but you don't have any really bad symptoms so you just shows up on

00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:58,080
blood work meaning so if you're diagnosing autoimmune disease shown up on blood work or you don't have

00:01:58,080 --> 00:02:03,600
any bad symptoms or you don't have any tissue destruction that's in what's called silent autoimmunity

00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:10,080
or phase one stage one autoimmunity and that's probably what you were in. And you know you can get

00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:16,000
that under control and you can put it in remission. So you can cure an autoimmune disease but you can

00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:21,920
put it in remission for a long, long time. So that's probably what's going on. You know you

00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:26,960
when you were diagnosed with cancer you made a lot of dietary changes you made different lifestyle

00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:40,160
changes and that can really calm down an autoimmune disease too. So that's good news.

